NINAJ AWIN HISTORICAL ARCHIVE
RIGHTS AND REUSE NOTICE

Project origin
--------------
Ninaj Awin was a multidisciplinary research and educational project developed at
the Universidad Mayor de San Simón (UMSS), Cochabamba, Bolivia, in 2015.

This GitHub repository and website are a personal historical archive maintained
by Eduardo Di Santi. Ownership or maintenance of this repository does not imply
ownership of the Ninaj Awin project as an institutional project of UMSS, nor does
it imply ownership of every photograph, video, software contribution, document,
model, graphic, recording, or other item preserved here.

Public availability
-------------------
The archive is made publicly accessible for historical, educational, scholarly,
and citation purposes.

PUBLIC AVAILABILITY DOES NOT PLACE THE CONTENT IN THE PUBLIC DOMAIN AND DOES NOT
GRANT A GENERAL LICENSE TO REPRODUCE, REDISTRIBUTE, MODIFY, REPUBLISH, EXHIBIT,
SELL, SUBLICENSE, INCORPORATE INTO DATASETS, USE FOR MACHINE-LEARNING TRAINING,
OR OTHERWISE REUSE THE MATERIAL.

